18:["$","aside",null,{"className":"docs_toc__B_lbZ","aria-label":"On this page","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"ON THIS PAGE"}],[["$","a","choose-the-right-layer",{"href":"#choose-the-right-layer","children":"Choose the right layer"}],["$","a","diagram-hit-miss-and-version-change",{"href":"#diagram-hit-miss-and-version-change","children":"Diagram: hit, miss, and version change"}],["$","a","implementation-put-each-cache-at-a-deliberate-boundary",{"href":"#implementation-put-each-cache-at-a-deliberate-boundary","children":"Implementation: put each cache at a deliberate boundary"}],["$","a","engineering-exercise",{"href":"#engineering-exercise","children":"Engineering exercise"}],["$","a","design-review-questions",{"href":"#design-review-questions","children":"Design review questions"}],["$","a","read-further",{"href":"#read-further","children":"Read further"}]]]}]
19:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"LESSON 05 OF 10"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Caching and invalidation"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":["A ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"cache"}]," keeps a reusable copy near the next reader. It reduces latency and work on an origin, but introduces a freshness contract. “Use a cache” is incomplete until the key, owner, lifetime, invalidation trigger, and behavior after a miss are defined."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"choose-the-right-layer","children":"Choose the right layer"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["A CDN or edge cache is a good fit for public, immutable images and versioned JavaScript. Private document bodies require careful permission handling and usually should not be stored in a shared public cache. Browser caches can revalidate with ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"ETag"}]," and ",["$","code","code-1",{"children":"If-None-Match"}],"; an unchanged representation can return ",["$","code","code-2",{"children":"304 Not Modified"}],". An application cache might hold document metadata or a search result, keyed by tenant, viewer permissions, query, and data version. The key must encode all inputs that affect the result."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":["For document 42, a safe simple policy is: on a successful edit, increment ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"version"}]," in the primary transaction; cache the body under ",["$","code","code-1",{"children":"document:42:v7"}]," instead of overwriting ",["$","code","code-2",{"children":"document:42"}],". The response for version 8 uses a new key, so old cached bytes cannot masquerade as the new version. Old keys expire. A listing may tolerate a short TTL; the editor's immediate post-save read should use the primary or a session-aware path."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":["If many misses for the same popular key arrive together, all may hit the database: a ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"cache stampede"}],". Bound concurrent fills per key, use short stale-while-revalidate only where stale data is acceptable, and size the origin for a realistic miss storm. A 95% hit ratio at 1,160 RPS still sends about 58 requests/second to the origin; the number can jump to 1,160 when the cache is cold."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"diagram-hit-miss-and-version-change","children":"Diagram: hit, miss, and version change"}],"\n",["$","figure","p-4",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/scale-design/caching.svg","alt":"A cache hit serves a versioned document; a miss reads the origin, and an edit creates a new versioned cache key.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"A cache hit serves a versioned document; a miss reads the origin, and an edit creates a new versioned cache key."}]]}],"\n",["$","details","pre-0",{"className":"docs_textDiagram__KfHuf","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Read the text version of this flow"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-aosdf-diagram","children":"GET doc v7 ──▶ cache v7 ── hit ──▶ response\n                   └── miss ──▶ primary + object store ──▶ fill\nEDIT doc ──▶ commit v8 ──▶ future reads use cache v8\n"}]}]]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"implementation-put-each-cache-at-a-deliberate-boundary","children":"Implementation: put each cache at a deliberate boundary"}],"\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e"],false]}]]}],"$L2f"]}]
